ion succeeded (no validation error) and the resulting generated preview showed unresolved placeholders verbatim: 'Hello {{customerName}}, your order {{orderId}} has shipped.'\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-29\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Duplicate field labels not rejected or disambiguated\", \"actual\": \"Adding a second field labeled 'clientName' (duplicate of an existing field) was silently accepted; the field-definition list in the submit dialog only showed 2 fields (deduplicated view), but after submission the template's fill form actually rendered 3 inputs: 'clientName *' (required), 'startDate', and a second unlabeled-asterisk 'clientName' input, both sharing colliding data-semtag-id 'preview.fields.item.clientname' and triggering additional console errors (React duplicate key warnings)\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing 'Resu' (4 chars) surfaced a suggestion 'Professional Resume'; clicking it filled search box with 'Professional Resume' and narrowed grid to 1 matching result\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search, category filter, scenario filter, favorites toggle, and sort selection all updated filters.result-count and templates.grid order/content instantly without any page navigation/reload (URL remained http://localhost:6089/ throughout)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-22\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"preview.missing-fields observable listed 'Please fill in: Full Name, Job Title, Email, ...' and Preview Result tab was disabled until fields filled\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-24\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Immediately after clicking favorite toggle, toggle state changed to 'on', header favorites label updated to 'Favorites 1', and favorites.count observable updated to '1'\"}, {\"item_id\": \"